      ":question/id": "7055556b-fdd2-5518-9d01-4c42a924c1d7",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={5}^{x}\\log _{7} (x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{5^{x}}{x \\ln{\\left(7 \\right)}}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={5}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\log _{7} (x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={({5}^{x})}^{′}\\log _{7} (x)+{5}^{x}{(\\log _{7} (x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({5}^{x}\\ln  (5))(\\log _{7} (x))+({5}^{x})(\\frac{1}{x\\ln  (7)}) \\\\  & ={5}^{x}\\ln  (5)\\log _{7} (x)+\\frac{{5}^{x}}{x\\ln  (7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b39264e0-6c61-517a-9b4b-21b85fcfc920",
